2026-11-19T17:38:02.1511324Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1511854Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1512535Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1514322Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1515613Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py --emit-prelude OUT "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1516315Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1516698Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1517356Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1517991Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1518604Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1519188Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1519785Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1520391Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1520902Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1521124Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1521419Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1522008Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1522579Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1523197Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1523439Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1524095Z ``--emit-prelude OUT`` writes to OUT the earlier top-level statements the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1524693Z block reads, found by running it until no ``NameError`` is left: each missing
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1525271Z name takes its last binding before the use (before the block, or before the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1525821Z prelude statement that needed it at module level). Run the block with
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1526377Z ``--prelude 'exec(open("OUT").read())'``. It derives from the tree it runs on,
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1526939Z so a mutant run needs no hand-copied prelude; exits 0 once the block runs
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1527516Z without raising (its checks are not judged), 1 on a name no earlier statement
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1527966Z binds or on any other exception.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1528141Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1528431Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1528978Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1529276Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1529582Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1529951Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1530688Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1531395Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py --emit-prelude OUT "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1531769Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1532061Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1532647Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1533221Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1534129Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1534687Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1535236Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1535820Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1536288Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1536509Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1536804Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1537494Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1538051Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1538537Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1538773Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1539038Z ``--emit-prelude OUT`` writes to OUT the earlier top-level statements the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1539613Z block reads, found by running it until no ``NameError`` is left: each missing
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1540237Z name takes its last binding before the use (before the block, or before the
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1540785Z prelude statement that needed it at module level). Run the block with
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1541330Z ``--prelude 'exec(open("OUT").read())'``. It derives from the tree it runs on,
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1541878Z so a mutant run needs no hand-copied prelude; exits 0 once the block runs
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1542459Z without raising (its checks are not judged), 1 on a name no earlier statement
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1542898Z binds or on any other exception.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1543067Z 
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1543351Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-19T17:38:02.1543961Z 
